{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 8398427a: all three choices accepted, with one\nduty on the first. The one export is `judgeActBody`, with the\nsignature that you state.\n\n1. Missing intent: accepted. When execution reaches a need for the\n   signed intent, the body answers `unavailable` and lacks the\n   intent. It gives no partial effects. The three needs are an\n   operand that reads the signed input, the cause of a creation\n   send, and the `given` of a Native rule. Fabricate no intent,\n   digest or cause. Add no Contract reason. Design no input port\n   for Native rules now.\n   The duty: the E1 note lists each act of Grow, Lending and\n   Counter that this rule makes `unavailable`, by definition and\n   act name. An act that creates a scope is on that list. If an\n   act of the reservation, the pinboard or the map is on it, tell\n   me before the E1 gate. A symbolic cause is the later answer. It\n   waits with the general symbolic effects of section 14.\n2. Symbol metadata and counts: accepted. The private optional\n   callback records the index of each emitted `from: self` effect.\n   The body returns those indexes and the selected signer beside\n   the draft without its input. The counter gets a body arm with no\n   envelope. The runtime passes no callback, and its draft bytes\n   stay equal. The baseline fixture of a0a85c7e shows that.\n3. `judgesTime`: accepted. The body keeps the structural policy and\n   the present checks of grant expiry and observations. No read\n   set, and no invented `notAfter`.\n\nRuling fa103f71 answers request de0cd410. It agrees with item 2\nhere: the body takes no key, and `packages/client` turns the\n`from: self` indexes into `{ entry }` names with the source.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8398427a8488f4e230b10e103c8154d6fd386df8 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:02c1227e7dc1c04a96ab423dd34c58537b63a2f2, git:sha1:58